<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-LE MANS 24-HOURS FINAL PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-LE MANS 24-HOURS FINAL PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LE MANS, France 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading final placings</p>
<p>in the Le Mans 24 Hours motor race on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Michele Alboreto (Italy)/Stefan Johansson (Sweden)/Tom</p>
<p>Kristensen (Denmark) TWR Porsche-Joest 361 laps (average speed</p>
<p>204.186 kph)</p>
<p>2. Jean-Marc Gounon (France)/Pierre-Henri Raphanel</p>
<p>(France)/Anders Olofsson (Sweden) McLaren BMW F1GTR 1 lap behind</p>
<p>3. Peter Kox (Netherlands)/Roberto Ravaglia (Italy)/Eric Helary</p>
<p>(France) McLaren BMW F1GTR 3 laps</p>
<p>4. Didier Cottaz (France)/Jerome Policand (France)/Marc Goosens</p>
<p>(Belgium) Courage C41 25</p>
<p>5. Pedro Lamy (Portugal)/Patrice Goueslard (France)/Armin Hahne</p>
<p>(Germany) Porsche 911 GT1 30</p>
<p>6. Giampiero Moretti (Italy)/Didier Theys (Belgium)</p>
<p>/Massimiliano Papis (Italy) Ferrari 333 SP 40</p>
<p>7. Emmanuel Clerico (France)/Henri Pescarolo (France)</p>
<p>/Jean-Philippe Belloc (France) Courage C36 42</p>
<p>8. Pierluigi Martini (Italy)/Christian Pescatori (Italy)</p>
<p>/Antonio Hermann (Brazil) Porsche 911 GT1 44</p>
<p>9. Michel Neugarten (Belgium)/Guy Martinolle (France)</p>
<p>/Jean-Claude Lagniez (France) Porsche 911 GT2 54</p>
<p>10. Andy Pilgrim (U.S.)/Andre Ahrle (Germany)/Bruno Eichmann</p>
<p>(Switzerland) Porsche 911 GT2 55</p>
<p>Fastest lap: Kristensen, 3 minutes 45.068 seconds (average</p>
<p>speed of 217.534 kph</p>
</text>
